    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0775" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.01B11 Registration/9–2949</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Foreign Agents Registration Section of
                        the Department of Justice</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Chief of the Division of Eastern European Affairs of the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-29">September 29, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">Re: Amtorg Trading Corporation</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Reinhardt</hi>: As you have been advised
                    previously, this Section sent a letter to Amtorg Trading Corporation on August
                    29, 1949, reminding it again of its obligation to file a registration statement
                    with this Department under the Foreign Agents Registration Act. A copy of this
                    letter has been furnished to you for your files.</p>
                <p>By letter dated September 16, 1949, signed by A. Zakharov,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d457-f1"/> President, Amtorg Trading Corporation stated that it
                    wished to reiterate the position which it took in its letter of March 13,
                        1947<anchor n="2" xml:id="d457-f2"/> to the effect that Amtorg Trading
                    Corporation carries on purely private, non-political, financial and mercantile
                    activities solely in furtherance of bona fide trade and commerce with commercial
                    organizations in the U.S.S.R. In view of this claim, Amtorg again stated that it
                    believes the provisions of Section 3 (<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>) of the
                    Foreign Agents Registration <pb facs="0776" n="762" xml:id="pg762"/> Act applied
                    to it and therefore Amtorg Trading Corporation is not subject to
                    registration.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Foley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d457-f1" n="1" xml:id="d457-f1-content">
                <p>Alexey Vasilyevich Zakharov, who had also been Acting Chairman and Chairman of
                    the Government Purchasing Commission of the Soviet Union in the United States,
                    1948–1949.</p>
            </note>
